WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.433
Now to New

00:00:00.433 --> 00:00:01.067
York, where

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:01.835
former President

00:00:01.835 --> 00:00:04.437
Donald Trump is now invited to testify

00:00:04.471 --> 00:00:06.039
before a Manhattan grand jury.

00:00:06.039 --> 00:00:07.540
It's all part of their investigation

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:08.141
into alleged

00:00:08.141 --> 00:00:08.708
hush money

00:00:08.708 --> 00:00:09.776
payments to stormy

00:00:09.776 --> 00:00:11.845
Daniels during the 2016 election.

00:00:11.878 --> 00:00:13.513
So this is a potential sign

00:00:13.513 --> 00:00:15.148
that prosecutors are zeroing

00:00:15.148 --> 00:00:16.750
in on an indictment.

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:18.818
Let's turn now to CNN's Chris Cornell.

00:00:18.818 --> 00:00:20.120
Carol, what do you know

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:20.553
Well, that's right.

00:00:20.553 --> 00:00:21.054
So sources

00:00:21.054 --> 00:00:21.721
tell us that

00:00:21.721 --> 00:00:22.489
this invitation

00:00:22.489 --> 00:00:22.989
was made

00:00:22.989 --> 00:00:23.990
to the former president's

00:00:23.990 --> 00:00:25.158
lawyers in recent days

00:00:25.158 --> 00:00:26.860
to appear before the grand jury.

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:27.794
And this is a sign

00:00:27.794 --> 00:00:28.828
that this investigation

00:00:28.828 --> 00:00:30.163
is coming to a conclusion

00:00:30.163 --> 00:00:31.031
and that a decision

00:00:31.031 --> 00:00:33.033
of whether or not to seek an indictment

00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:34.134
is likely to happen

00:00:34.134 --> 00:00:36.202
more in the next few weeks than months.

00:00:36.603 --> 00:00:37.337
You know, we've also seen

00:00:37.337 --> 00:00:38.338
a parade of witnesses

00:00:38.338 --> 00:00:40.440
going in Kellyanne Conway, Hope Hicks,

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:40.640
you know,

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:41.241
all signals

00:00:41.241 --> 00:00:42.709
that this is getting toward

00:00:42.709 --> 00:00:44.411
the finish line.

00:00:44.411 --> 00:00:46.413
Also today, Michael Cohen went in to meet

00:00:46.413 --> 00:00:47.814
with the district attorney's office.

00:00:47.814 --> 00:00:49.649
Our cameras caught him.

00:00:49.649 --> 00:00:50.583
And let's take a listen

00:00:50.583 --> 00:00:51.484
to what he had to say.

00:00:53.953 --> 00:00:55.989
I have to applaud

00:00:55.989 --> 00:00:57.557
District Attorney Bragg

00:00:57.557 --> 00:00:58.358
for giving Donald

00:00:58.358 --> 00:00:59.659
the opportunity to come in

00:00:59.659 --> 00:01:00.493
and to tell his story.

00:01:00.493 --> 00:01:01.628
Now, knowing Donald

00:01:01.628 --> 00:01:02.929
as well as I do,

00:01:02.929 --> 00:01:04.297
understand that

00:01:04.297 --> 00:01:05.832
he doesn't tell the truth.

00:01:05.832 --> 00:01:06.866
It's one thing to turn around

00:01:06.866 --> 00:01:08.768
and to lie on your untruths, social.

00:01:08.768 --> 00:01:10.203
It's another thing to turn around

00:01:10.203 --> 00:01:11.671
and lie before a grand jury,

00:01:11.671 --> 00:01:12.872
which I don't suspect

00:01:12.872 --> 00:01:15.008
that he's going to be coming.

00:01:15.442 --> 00:01:15.909
Now, sources

00:01:15.909 --> 00:01:17.277
tell us that among the charges

00:01:17.277 --> 00:01:18.311
that prosecutors are weighing,

00:01:18.311 --> 00:01:20.146
they relate to the hush money payment.

00:01:20.146 --> 00:01:21.014
But hush money payment

00:01:21.014 --> 00:01:21.881
itself is not a crime.

00:01:21.881 --> 00:01:23.616
So they're looking at how this payment

00:01:23.616 --> 00:01:24.451
was reimbursed.

00:01:24.451 --> 00:01:25.518
Remember, Donald Trump

00:01:25.518 --> 00:01:27.620
signed those checks to Michael Cohen.

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:28.922
So prosecutors are looking at

00:01:28.922 --> 00:01:30.390
how the Trump Organization

00:01:30.390 --> 00:01:31.524
accounted for that

00:01:31.524 --> 00:01:32.792
in their books and records.

00:01:32.792 --> 00:01:33.893
So they're looking at possible

00:01:33.893 --> 00:01:35.562
falsifying business record charge,

00:01:35.562 --> 00:01:36.696
which is a misdemeanor,

00:01:36.696 --> 00:01:38.798
or falsifying records in

00:01:38.798 --> 00:01:40.934
order to commit or conceal another crime.

00:01:40.934 --> 00:01:41.601
In this case,

00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:42.735
that could be campaign

00:01:42.735 --> 00:01:44.204
finance violations now.

00:01:44.204 --> 00:01:45.939
I mean, this is not an easy case.

00:01:45.939 --> 00:01:47.207
It's a novel legal theory.

00:01:47.207 --> 00:01:47.607
And Trump's

00:01:47.607 --> 00:01:49.042
lawyers will certainly have

00:01:49.042 --> 00:01:49.909
a lot of defenses

00:01:49.909 --> 00:01:51.444
that they'll throw up at this.

00:01:51.444 --> 00:01:53.046
We spoke to one of the attorneys,

00:01:53.046 --> 00:01:54.147
Joe Tacopina.

00:01:54.147 --> 00:01:56.116
And in a statement, he said, the D.A.

00:01:56.116 --> 00:01:56.983
and the former D.A.

00:01:56.983 --> 00:01:58.985
have been scouring every aspect

00:01:58.985 --> 00:02:00.820
of President Trump's personal life

00:02:00.820 --> 00:02:01.788
and business affairs

00:02:01.788 --> 00:02:03.690
for years in search of a crime

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:04.958
and needs to stop.

00:02:04.958 --> 00:02:05.892
This is simply not

00:02:05.892 --> 00:02:07.694
what our justice system is about.

00:02:07.694 --> 00:02:08.661
And as we know, Trump

00:02:08.661 --> 00:02:09.662
is facing a number

00:02:09.662 --> 00:02:11.431
of other legal challenges,

00:02:11.431 --> 00:02:12.866
other criminal investigations

00:02:12.866 --> 00:02:14.000
having to do with the 2020

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:15.368
election, both in Fulton

00:02:15.368 --> 00:02:16.069
County, Florida

00:02:16.069 --> 00:02:17.370
and at the Justice Department level,

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:18.238
as well as the handling

00:02:18.238 --> 00:02:19.239
of classified documents.

00:02:19.239 --> 00:02:21.474
So certainly a lot coming to a head

00:02:21.474 --> 00:02:22.408
for the former president.

00:02:22.408 --> 00:02:23.343
This one looks like

00:02:23.343 --> 00:02:24.811
it could be the first move

00:02:24.811 --> 00:02:26.212
a long time coming to.

00:02:26.212 --> 00:02:28.081
Chris, Cornell, thank you.

00:02:28.081 --> 00:02:28.948
Well, let's bring in legal

00:02:28.948 --> 00:02:30.316
analyst Elliot Williams.

00:02:30.316 --> 00:02:31.518
So, Elliott,

00:02:31.518 --> 00:02:33.019
the president has been offered

00:02:33.019 --> 00:02:34.921
an opportunity to testify.

00:02:34.921 --> 00:02:36.122
Does that the former president,

00:02:36.122 --> 00:02:37.023
does that signal

00:02:37.023 --> 00:02:38.057
that an indictment, in your

00:02:38.057 --> 00:02:38.825
view, is likely

00:02:40.026 --> 00:02:42.595
and signals that one could be coming now?

00:02:42.962 --> 00:02:45.131
New York is one of the jurisdictions,

00:02:45.298 --> 00:02:46.299
and there are any number across

00:02:46.299 --> 00:02:47.100
the United States

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:47.967
that give defendants

00:02:47.967 --> 00:02:49.435
and operative or potential defendants

00:02:49.435 --> 00:02:50.803
an opportunity to come in

00:02:50.803 --> 00:02:52.205
and make their case prior

00:02:52.205 --> 00:02:53.873
to charges being raised.

00:02:53.873 --> 00:02:56.142
Now, sometimes people can use that

00:02:56.142 --> 00:02:56.910
as an opportunity

00:02:56.910 --> 00:02:57.911
to sort of say, you know, look,

00:02:57.911 --> 00:02:59.913
I might have engaged in those actions,

00:02:59.913 --> 00:03:00.680
but here's why.

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:01.748
And there's a legal basis

00:03:01.748 --> 00:03:03.216
for why I did them and so on.

00:03:03.216 --> 00:03:03.616
The problem is

00:03:03.616 --> 00:03:05.018
that it's fraught with peril

00:03:05.018 --> 00:03:05.652
to do that,

00:03:05.652 --> 00:03:06.853
because, number one,

00:03:06.853 --> 00:03:07.921
he would have to waive

00:03:07.921 --> 00:03:09.422
what's called his immunity.

00:03:09.422 --> 00:03:10.190
So any statement

00:03:10.190 --> 00:03:11.958
he made could be used against him.

00:03:11.958 --> 00:03:12.458
And number two,

00:03:12.458 --> 00:03:13.626
he can't control the questions

00:03:13.626 --> 00:03:14.194
that he's asked.

00:03:14.194 --> 00:03:15.862
So for any number of reasons,

00:03:15.862 --> 00:03:17.630
we're probably not likely to see him

00:03:17.630 --> 00:03:20.233
come in and testify here.

00:03:20.233 --> 00:03:23.236
So Kerry described this as a novel

00:03:23.503 --> 00:03:25.004
legal theory.

00:03:25.004 --> 00:03:27.307
Does novel, in this case,

00:03:27.307 --> 00:03:29.142
equal week case?

00:03:29.142 --> 00:03:31.211
What's your take on on the approach here?

00:03:32.212 --> 00:03:34.280
That's an excellent question, Victor.

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:35.548
And look at the way

00:03:35.548 --> 00:03:37.684
our law works in this country

00:03:37.684 --> 00:03:39.352
is that you bring cases

00:03:39.352 --> 00:03:41.588
based on what has come before.

00:03:41.588 --> 00:03:44.090
And there are some cases that simply

00:03:44.424 --> 00:03:45.291
the situation hasn't

00:03:45.291 --> 00:03:46.092
presented itself before.

00:03:46.092 --> 00:03:47.560
And it's legally complex.

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:49.996
And the backup cameras point.

00:03:50.230 --> 00:03:51.898
It's sort of a case within a case.

00:03:51.898 --> 00:03:52.432
Within a case,

00:03:52.432 --> 00:03:53.533
you would have to prove first

00:03:53.533 --> 00:03:55.068
that there were hush money payments,

00:03:55.068 --> 00:03:56.035
but then

00:03:56.035 --> 00:03:57.870
not just that the payments happened,

00:03:57.870 --> 00:03:59.272
that they happened in

00:03:59.272 --> 00:04:00.773
knowing furtherance

00:04:00.773 --> 00:04:02.242
of another criminal offense.

00:04:02.242 --> 00:04:03.343
So it's not just

00:04:03.343 --> 00:04:04.177
writing a hush money

00:04:04.177 --> 00:04:06.512
check to to quiet down

00:04:06.512 --> 00:04:07.847
somebody who might have

00:04:07.847 --> 00:04:09.215
embarrassing facts about you.

00:04:09.215 --> 00:04:10.083
It's because, you know,

00:04:10.083 --> 00:04:12.051
you're violating campaign finance law.

00:04:12.051 --> 00:04:13.419
That's never been done.

00:04:13.419 --> 00:04:14.520
And that's a big leap

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:15.588
and a big step

00:04:15.588 --> 00:04:16.389
for what

00:04:16.389 --> 00:04:17.657
ultimately could be a misdemeanor

00:04:17.657 --> 00:04:18.891
or a very, very small penalty.

00:04:18.891 --> 00:04:20.126
That doesn't even Gary

00:04:20.126 --> 00:04:20.927
doesn't require

00:04:20.927 --> 00:04:22.562
is it required to carry jail time.

00:04:22.562 --> 00:04:24.297
So, yes, they can do it.

00:04:24.297 --> 00:04:25.765
And there's certainly

00:04:25.765 --> 00:04:27.066
a path to it happening.

00:04:27.066 --> 00:04:28.001
But it's not

00:04:28.001 --> 00:04:30.103
particularly straightforward legally.

00:04:30.103 --> 00:04:30.336
Yeah.

00:04:30.336 --> 00:04:32.272
Talk more about the potential charges,

00:04:32.272 --> 00:04:33.439
because it could range anything

00:04:33.439 --> 00:04:35.441
from a misdemeanor to a felony.

00:04:35.441 --> 00:04:37.110
So in terms of sentences

00:04:37.110 --> 00:04:39.145
that they may carry

00:04:39.145 --> 00:04:40.747
what's on the horizon here?

00:04:41.881 --> 00:04:42.315
Sure.

00:04:42.315 --> 00:04:43.616
Starting with the felony.

00:04:43.616 --> 00:04:45.051
Even if so, let's pretend

00:04:45.051 --> 00:04:45.918
that the prosecutors

00:04:45.918 --> 00:04:47.754
even are able to establish

00:04:47.754 --> 00:04:48.554
all these hush money

00:04:48.554 --> 00:04:50.723
payments were made to suppress

00:04:50.723 --> 00:04:52.292
or to suppress

00:04:52.292 --> 00:04:54.460
or commit a campaign finance violation.

00:04:54.661 --> 00:04:56.062
Even that has a maximum

00:04:56.062 --> 00:04:57.030
four year sentence.

00:04:57.030 --> 00:04:58.898
And nobody gets a four year sentence

00:04:58.898 --> 00:05:00.433
for a campaign finance violation,

00:05:00.433 --> 00:05:01.434
and it's not even required

00:05:01.434 --> 00:05:02.502
to send them to jail.

00:05:02.502 --> 00:05:03.236
So it would be

00:05:03.236 --> 00:05:04.537
maybe for probation

00:05:04.537 --> 00:05:06.439
or something like that.

00:05:06.439 --> 00:05:08.141
That's a lot of legal wrangling

00:05:08.141 --> 00:05:08.875
to go through for

00:05:08.875 --> 00:05:10.977
somebody that may never end up

00:05:10.977 --> 00:05:13.513
going to jail in the first place. So.

00:05:13.513 --> 00:05:14.781
And then if that doesn't happen,

00:05:14.781 --> 00:05:15.782
it's just a misdemeanor,

00:05:15.782 --> 00:05:17.183
which doesn't even carry

00:05:17.183 --> 00:05:18.851
less than a year in prison.

00:05:18.851 --> 00:05:20.953
So there's just not significant penalties

00:05:20.953 --> 00:05:22.722
that even under the best of circumstances

00:05:22.722 --> 00:05:24.390
would come from this case.

00:05:24.390 --> 00:05:25.892
Let's talk about Michael Cohen.

00:05:25.892 --> 00:05:26.759
We just heard from him

00:05:26.759 --> 00:05:28.461
he was there at the Manhattan DA's

00:05:28.461 --> 00:05:29.395
office today.

00:05:29.395 --> 00:05:30.363
A source tells CNN

00:05:30.363 --> 00:05:32.098
he'll be back there Monday.

00:05:32.098 --> 00:05:33.800
And it's been pointed out that, yes, he's

00:05:33.800 --> 00:05:35.101
a convicted felon.

00:05:35.101 --> 00:05:36.269
He's a proven liar.

00:05:36.269 --> 00:05:39.672
But he he lied on behalf of Trump.

00:05:40.206 --> 00:05:40.540
Right.

00:05:40.540 --> 00:05:43.376
How problematic is that for this case

00:05:43.376 --> 00:05:44.277
and how much of the case

00:05:44.277 --> 00:05:47.280
really hinges upon Michael Cohen's word?

00:05:48.681 --> 00:05:49.048
Sure.

00:05:49.048 --> 00:05:49.549
Well, based

00:05:49.549 --> 00:05:49.816
on what's

00:05:49.816 --> 00:05:50.650
publicly available

00:05:50.650 --> 00:05:51.417
right now,

00:05:51.417 --> 00:05:53.419
the strongest evidence they have

00:05:53.419 --> 00:05:54.420
is Michael Cohen's word.

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:55.521
And I want to be clear.

00:05:55.521 --> 00:05:58.458
He testified under oath before Congress

00:05:58.458 --> 00:06:00.793
as to the facts of this

00:06:01.694 --> 00:06:02.528
of this case here.

00:06:02.528 --> 00:06:04.530
So that itself is powerful.

00:06:04.530 --> 00:06:05.732
Evidence is under oath.

00:06:05.732 --> 00:06:07.367
It's more and so on.

00:06:07.367 --> 00:06:08.368
The simple fact is

00:06:08.368 --> 00:06:10.370
he is a convicted felon

00:06:10.370 --> 00:06:12.271
based on honesty issues.

00:06:12.271 --> 00:06:14.307
And any defense attorney

00:06:14.307 --> 00:06:15.708
is going to hammer him

00:06:15.708 --> 00:06:16.442
and hammer

00:06:16.442 --> 00:06:17.710
a prosecution here

00:06:17.710 --> 00:06:20.613
over the fact that the star witness

00:06:20.613 --> 00:06:21.881
has serious credibility issues.

00:06:21.881 --> 00:06:23.015
So, you know,

00:06:23.015 --> 00:06:24.350
when Karen mentioned earlier

00:06:24.350 --> 00:06:25.184
in the segment

00:06:25.184 --> 00:06:25.952
that they were bringing

00:06:25.952 --> 00:06:27.720
in a number of other witnesses

00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:28.955
and trying to get other evidence,

00:06:28.955 --> 00:06:30.456
I think that's to insulate

00:06:30.456 --> 00:06:31.290
around the fact

00:06:31.290 --> 00:06:32.825
that the evidence that you have

00:06:32.825 --> 00:06:34.527
and Michael Cohen just isn't that strong.

00:06:34.527 --> 00:06:35.928
He might be telling the truth,

00:06:35.928 --> 00:06:37.196
but he's got credibility issues.

00:06:37.196 --> 00:06:38.030
And in court,

00:06:38.030 --> 00:06:39.399
all that matters

00:06:39.399 --> 00:06:40.400
is can a jury

00:06:40.400 --> 00:06:40.967
believe

00:06:40.967 --> 00:06:42.435
the evidence is presented to them?

00:06:42.435 --> 00:06:44.137
And when they have a witness

00:06:44.137 --> 00:06:45.271
who will himself

00:06:45.271 --> 00:06:45.972
admit on the stand

00:06:45.972 --> 00:06:47.440
that he's got a felony conviction,

00:06:47.440 --> 00:06:49.041
it's just hard to believe them in

00:06:49.041 --> 00:06:49.709
order to convict.

